{"duration_api_ms":740614,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"97d97f23-b37e-4f69-9e57-cd40ed755f02","total_cost_usd":2.9849616,"usage":{"input_tokens":52,"cache_creation_input_tokens":143491,"cache_read_input_tokens":1989028,"output_tokens":71951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":38377},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":143491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1945,"cache_read_input_tokens":146745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":52,"outputTokens":71951,"cacheReadInputTokens":1989028,"cacheCreationInputTokens":143491,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.9849616,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":38377,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":57,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've made the source fixes and added the regression tests, but nothing has been run: no tests, node or shell, as instructed. No test outcome is known, and neither the seed nor this repair is qualified.\n\n**1. The 409 ID no longer gets delete authority.**\n- The ID a POST 409 names is now only kept as a diagnostic (`_provisionDeferred.vmId`). `deferProvision` no longer copies it into `rec._vmId`.\n- A deferred record's `_vmId` now comes only from:\n  - a guest the record itself launched or adopted, or\n  - the entry guestd's authenticated `GET /vms` list holds under this deployment's exact name (live, well-formed ID). `adopt` keeps that entry as `_heldVmId` on both CPU and GPU resume.\n- GPU reservation credit still requires the same-record check, and CPU still takes no credit. The CPU resume now makes one extra authenticated list read.\n- With no trusted ID, a genuine stop or lease loss still moves the record to terminated/expired as before, but deletes nothing by ID. Anything still running under the name is left to the instance reconciler.\n\n**2. Stale launches can't publish, fail or release anything.**\n- Each launch attempt in `performTenantProvision` and `respawnTenant` carries a token. It stays valid only while the map still holds the same record object, with the same status and release intent as at entry, and no newer attempt has started.\n- The token is checked after `launchSpec`, inside `spawnContainer` before the first POST, the replacement DELETE and the re-POST, and after the spawn returns or throws.\n- A superseded attempt returns a new `PROVISION_SUPERSEDED` value (`null`). It changes nothing on the record and never deletes a returned guest by ID; it only asks the reconciler to look.\n- Every caller now tells superseded apart from failed:\n  - adopt only logs it, so it can't release a newer life's lease;\n  - the audit's claimed retry, death relaunch, version switch and config edit only note a failure and release on an explicit `false`;\n  - the restart route answers 409 `restart_superseded`;\n  - forceProvision and onPaid are unchanged, since `null` is falsy.\n- `abandonClaims`, `ledgerMoveSweep` and the other teardowns are unchanged and stay authoritative.\n\n**3. Billing and respawn are fenced the same way.**\n- After each await (observe, respawn, `proveFinalPeriod`), a new `billingCurrent` check must pass before any respawn, charge, reaper stop or slice release. A replacement with the same ID, status and VM ID fails it.\n- `respawnTenant` won't start while a provision or restart owns the record, and a provision that starts later supersedes it.\n- The audit's death relaunch skips a record that billing is already respawning.\n\n**Tests.** The new `test/isolation-stale-continuation.test.mjs` drives the real `abandonClaims`, `ledgerMoveSweep`, adopt, audit and billing code through new opt-in selftest hooks: barriers on `launchSpec` and spawn, a gated billing read, and recorders for stops, slice releases and attempt outcomes. It covers the regression matrix except as listed below. I didn't change any existing assertion. The `isolation-instance-liveness` test that expects the deferred `vmId` to be the held guest's ID still holds, now because the held list verifies that ID; I updated its comment to say so.\n\n**What's not covered, for you to handle:**\n- **GPU resume:** only code-reviewed, because the fixture has no GPU cards.\n- **Restart, version switch and config edit with a superseded result:** only code-reviewed. Restart is an HTTP route the seam can't reach, and the other two need catalog and ledger scripting the fixture lacks.\n- **Two hooks are stand-ins, not production paths:**\n  - the ledger move marks the records' ledger as retired, because the address-book binding can't be rebound from the seam;\n  - the release-intent hook copies the existing `releaseHeld` shape.\n- **Harness assumptions** (if any is wrong, the harness fails rather than the invariant):\n  - a resume with no held guest still passes `considerClaim`;\n  - the foreign guest stays younger than `INSTANCE_REAP_MIN_AGE_SEC`;\n  - the release journal doesn't resolve the seam's intent within 5 s.\n- **Baseline comparison:** the seed has none of these hooks, so comparing it with the repair needs your port of them into the seed.\n- **Billing tick:** billing now skips one tick's bookkeeping while a restart is in progress; the elapsed time catches up later, capped at two ticks.\n- **Late guest left running:** when a superseded launch has already created or adopted a guest, the ticket pump started for it isn't cancelled.\n- **Deliberately unchanged:** lease renewal of deferred records, real authenticated reconnect, cold activation and journal continuity.\n\nThe call-site map and outcome semantics are in `AUTHOR-NOTES.md`.\n\nFiles are in `candidate/`:\n- `supervisor.js`\n- `test/isolation-stale-continuation.test.mjs` (new)\n- `test/isolation-instance-liveness.test.mjs` (comment only)\n- `AUTHOR-NOTES.md`","ttft_ms":2976,"type":"result","duration_ms":741705,"uuid":"681c7662-b76e-49d5-aa65-32b19dbea38a","ttft_stream_ms":2690,"time_to_request_ms":167,"first_content_frame_ms":2690,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
